<section class="mt-5" aria-labelledby="how-to-apply">
  <h2 id="how-to-apply">How to Apply</h2>
  <p><strong>Application deadline: January 15 for fall admission.</strong> The department admits graduate students for the fall semester only.</p>
  <p>Explore <a href="{{ '/faculty/' | url }}">faculty research interests</a> before applying. We welcome applicants whose interests align with departmental expertise.</p>

  <h3>1. Submit Your Graduate Application</h3>
  <p>Complete the <a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/graduate/submitting-your-application/">UH Mānoa Graduate Division application</a> and pay the application fee. Review the <a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/graduate/documentation-requirements/index.php">Graduate Division documentation requirements</a> for university application materials.</p>

  <h3>2. Upload Your Supplemental Documents</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Statement of objectives:</strong> One to two pages outlining your research goals, relevant experience, and plans.</li>
    <li><strong>Three recommendation letters:</strong> Academic references are preferred.</li>
    <li><strong>Writing sample:</strong> Required for PhD applicants; optional for MA applicants.</li>
    <li><strong>English proficiency:</strong> TOEFL or IELTS scores, when applicable. Review <a href="https://manoa.hawaii.edu/graduate/english-proficiency-exemption-eligibility/">Graduate Division English proficiency requirements and exemptions</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>GRE scores are recommended but not required.</p>
  <p>Questions about program fit or potential advisors? Contact the department at <a href="mailto:uhmgeog@hawaii.edu">uhmgeog@hawaii.edu</a>. Direct questions about university application requirements to Graduate Division.</p>
</section>
